# Motion Law

**Principle:** Transitions should use consistent duration and easing. Align with Material Design motion guidelines.

## Duration Scale

| Use Case | Duration | Example |
|----------|----------|---------|
| Micro (hover, focus) | 150–200ms | Button hover |
| Standard (expand, fade) | 250–300ms | Dropdown, modal |
| Complex (layout shift) | 400–500ms | Accordion, carousel |
| Slow (page transition) | 500–600ms | Full-page |

**Preferred:** 200ms, 300ms, 400ms (align with 8pt-ish rhythm)

## Easing

- **Standard:** `cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)` — Material "standard"
- **Decelerate:** `cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.2, 1)` — enter animations
- **Accelerate:** `cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 1, 1)` — exit animations
- **Bounce:** `cubic-bezier(0.68, -0.55, 0.265, 1.55)` — playful feedback

**Avoid:** `linear` for UI (feels mechanical); `ease-in-out` without cubic-bezier (less predictable).

## When to Animate

- State changes (hover, active, focus)
- Expand/collapse (accordion, nav)
- Enter/exit (modals, toasts)
- Layout shifts (carousel slide)

**Avoid:** Animating on every scroll; excessive motion that distracts.

